## Summary

The victim host at **10.8.15.133** (DESKTOP-H8ALZBV, user plucero) was infected via a spear-phishing delivery from a fake FedEx domain (**quote.checkfedexexp.com**) on 2024-08-15 at 04:10:58. The infection led to installation of a **commodity RAT** that beacons persistently to **72.5.43.29:80**. The malware uses obfuscated payloads disguised as Windows updates and demonstrates typical RAT behavior: simple HTTP C2 protocol, bare-IP communication, repeated GET/POST beaconing, and secondary payload downloads. No signature-level detection is available from IDS alerts, so attribution is behavioral.
